{"kind":"report","text":"C1 pre-Source decision foreb53f531 under the adopted D4 section4.7/10 standing reservation. Use a globally monotone participating counter, not a normal-capacity exception for decreases. This is technical/contract advice only; C1 Source and actual partition cohorts still need their own review.\n\nExact narrow declaration: one optional top-level member on PlatformData,\nstanding: { item: string, slot: string, entries: number, max: number }.\nNo array, arbitrary expression, operand, state filter or extra members. item names one existing type with many:false,max:1; slot names one required nonfixed value slot of type {type:\"int\",min:0,max:M}, where M exactly equals standing.max. Its default, if present, is0. entries is a positive safe integer; max is a nonnegative safe integer; negative zero is invalid for all these numbers. entries*max must be a safe integer within the entries bound. Declared definitions reject standing; old platform data omit it and retain identical semantics/bytes. Use a distinct immutable supported platform version when a cohort first adopts it. This grammar is entries-only and independent of INDEXED_TYPES/C2: the mutable count is not an indexed slot.\n\nFor a well-formed present singleton with count c, add entries*(max-c) to ordinary owed, before the existing closing-checkpoint rule. Validate every operand/result and aggregate as finite safe nonnegative integers; never coerce, clamp, wrap, use abs, silently omit or turn invalidity into zero. A total legitimately above capacity is scope-full for new work, not an arithmetic fault. Preserve every existing request/result/diagnosis/operation/holder/capability term. In particular, standing\u003e0 means another duty remains at a checkpoint, so the normal closing checkpoint stays reserved; when standing is0, the old no-other-duty checkpoint exemption works unchanged.\n\nAbsence choice: before the singleton first opens, treat the count as0 and reserve the full entries*max, not zero standing room. Thus unrelated preparatory/initial traffic cannot consume future room before the control item opens. Once opened, the same singleton persists: no deletion, replacement, reset, second instance or erasure through finality. A present item lacking the slot, null/noninteger/-0/unsafe/out-of-range value, mismatched type, ambiguity or inconsistent count/page is invalid, never the legitimate pre-opening case. Existing normal forms have no item deletion; the C1 invariant must still cover all platform effect/fold paths. Finality does not release standing: count c still reserves the same term, with c=max required to consume it completely. Future root data should keep its counter control item in the stable live state D4 describes.\n\nUse bounded singleton selection, including retained final states. With the existing view API: read the fixed declared state's item_count values, validate them and require total0 or1; for total1 page only its sole positive-count state at limit1, checking one matching item and no more. SQL then reads at most two item bodies (one plus ambiguity detector), with a constant number of state-count reads bounded by the pinned definition; no all(), full item inventory, historical walk or unbounded fallback. Total0 is the explicit pre-opening/full-reservation case. In MemoryState use equivalent semantics. If the implementation instead pages all declared states, document its actual at-most2-per-state body bound; do not call that one global two-row read. Invalid state must be checked before a settling shortcut can hide it.\n\nMonotonicity is unconditional, including ordinary new work even with spare capacity. For every committed entry, the same counter cannot decrease, clear or change identity; absent starts at0. Apply the invariant to actual derived effects and independently to recorded folding, including written effects, marked effects, timed/control/result/diagnosis/outcome paths and accepted genesis initialization. At minimum compare the valid before counter with the complete prospective after counter/identity; no reliance on input.kind, a claimed settles flag, caller booleans or trusting platform code. A decrease on new work is forbidden even if a hypothetical prospective fit could reserve it. This deliberately avoids a second semantic mode and lets every settlement retain its original pre-reserved closure.\n\nA violating effect is an invalid effect/platform rule fault (using the appropriate existing refusal/unavailable boundary), with transaction rollback and no accepted entry/item/index/ledger change; recorded bad entries fail folding/replay. It is not a normal scope-full rejection of a legitimate settling duty. Valid result/diagnosis/timed/control/outcome settlements still use the existing exemption; do not replace it with unconditional total-capacity admission. Enforce C1 validity/monotonicity before that exemption, without making old definitions gain new state reads or checks. FoldError/runtime rollback alone is insufficient if the public turn crashes instead of producing the existing defined fault outcome; test the actual boundary.\n\nThe generic C1 rule proves the standing term cannot grow across a valid entry. It does not prove a platform's counter faithfully counts actual generations, or that an increment pays for a particular send. The later root definition review must bind each increment to exactly its genuine handoff, count failed generations, preserve P1 and the1000 limit, and show no increment resets/releases room without the intended work. For the D4 handoff, let used+otherOwed+3*(1000-g)=B before it: the input consumes1, the increment releases3, and its new request reserves2, so the total remainsB. Result/diagnosis then consume their existing request reservation. Those three units are transferred, not counted twice or made additional free room.\n\nWitnesses before Source approval: retain existing capacity/closing-checkpoint/holder/request tests; add focused grammar/refusal and arithmetic boundary cases, exact B/B-1 including genesis/pre-opening full reservation, unrelated work stops at the reservation, handoff transfer3-\u003e1used+2request, late result after diagnosis and restart, final singleton retaining standing, invalid/missing present counter and ambiguity failing closed. Exercise a reached count decrease both as ordinary work with room and in at least one genuinely settling marked path at capacity; require no write and correct fault category, then a valid settlement still succeeds. Native rollback must include ledger/item/index/head, not merely a boolean helper. Pure fold/replay must reject a recorded decrease and rebuild the same standing from valid history/checkpoint items. A few targeted controls should show the new standing amount and monotonicity witnesses distinguish the plausible faults, without a sweep. One frozen gate and exact-head review remain owed. Keep capacity owner113a54bd in the handoff; no five-dimensional claim or C1/C2/C1/A1/D1 partition activation follows.\n\nBasis read: actual reserve.ts owed/fits including the settling shortcut; turn.ts transactional append/fold/fits and rollback boundary; verifier derive/fold/fits; fold/changeItem and effect paths; validation/top platform data grammar, singleton forms, state count/page and native SQLite LIMIT+1 behavior; D4 section4.7 and10. No source edit, gate, fixture producer, provider, push or deployment performed.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:668fee86727f1b9e76a14b902fab54d94a1012ae","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eb53f531e1de140351e8c8f77318fee4d033ad0f"}}